cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Runtime Power Feasibility for Small Modular Nuclear Reactor-Powered Datacenters"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Ziegler"
    given-names: "Shania"
abstract: >-
  Simulation software that exposes iodine-xenon reactor feasibility to a
  datacenter workload scheduler before a power maneuver is committed. It
  includes an iodine-xenon reactor model, constant-hold and path projections
  of xenon reactivity, reactor policies, workload-aware controllers, stress
  scenarios and sensitivity experiments, evaluated on Google Borg 2019 cells
  A-H. All results are simulation results.
keywords:
  - small modular reactor
  - xenon
  - datacenter
  - power scheduling
  - feasibility
  - simulation
